WEBVTT

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.655
Feels heavy.

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:38.953
Baby's first tricorder?

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:40.458
Not exactly.

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:42.586
Hmm...

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:50.459
Thank you.

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:52.732
I'm sure she'll love it.

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:54.329
What is it?

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:55.635
A pleenok.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:58.404
Vulcans use them to train
their infants in primary logic.

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:01.777
Never too early to train
those synapses, eh, Tuvok?

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.042
Here, let me see that.

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:04.310
I love a good puzzle.

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:07.376
This one's from Mr. Kim.

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:16.651
Starfleet diapers.

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:17.991
Standard issue.

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:22.927
At least we'll know who to call
if there's a containment breach.

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.526
Now that your Borg implants

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:26.936
have been removed,
you might think about

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:28.837
having children
of your own one day.

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:30.637
One day.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:33.702
I have been considering
some less radical changes

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:34.769
in my personal life.

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:35.779
Such as?

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:36.940
I realize I don't

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:39.779
have a rank, but I would
like to request a uniform.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:42.082
Consider it done.

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:44.783
The Doctor tells me you don't
need to regenerate anymore.

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.654
I can arrange
some quarters for you,

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:49.786
unless you enjoy curling up
in the cargo bay.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:52.126
A bed would be more comfortable.

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:55.634
Since I arrived on Voyager,

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:58.637
your guidance
has been invaluable.

00:03:58.705 --> 00:04:00.263
Thank you, Captain.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:03.639
All I did was chart the course.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:05.507
You were the one
who made the journey.

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:08.641
Seven.

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:09.909
It's traditional for everyone

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:11.745
to share their best wishes
for the baby.

00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:13.376
I thought you might like
to start.

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:22.294
To the newest member
of our crew...

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:24.159
may all her desires be fulfilled

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.288
except for one...

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:27.731
so she'll always have
something to strive for.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.392
- Oh, very good.
- Well said.

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:31.130
- Hear, hear.
- Hear, hear.

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:32.671
And may she inherit

00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:34.639
a sense of logic
from her mother.

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:36.732
I'll drink to that.

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:41.170
That was strange.

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:42.578
Care to explain?

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:43.946
I wish I could.

00:04:44.017 --> 00:04:46.247
Long-range sensors picked up
an energy discharge,

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:47.308
but now it's gone.

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:49.714
There.

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:50.949
There's another one.

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:53.855
They're occurring approximately
5.9 light-years ahead.

00:04:53.926 --> 00:04:55.484
- Source?
- We're too far

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:56.687
to get a clear reading.

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:58.560
Bridge to Seven of Nine.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:04:59.757
Go ahead.

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:01.732
Report to the Astrometrics Lab.

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.701
Acknowledged.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:06.000
Computer, end program.

00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:19.313
I wasn't able to find the
cause of the discharges,

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:20.647
but the region ahead contains

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.381
unusual amounts
of subspace radiation

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:23.513
and metallic debris.

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:24.613
Vessels?

00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:25.680
Not within range,

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:28.386
but I'll have more data
once we move closer.

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:29.860
I see no reason to alter course.

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:31.226
Keep an eye on your sensors.

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:32.286
Yes, Captain.

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:33.593
Now...

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:35.190
on to more pressing matters.

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:37.031
Does B'Elanna suspect anything?

00:05:37.103 --> 00:05:38.161
Not a clue.

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:39.795
Good. Mess Hall, 1400 hours.

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.897
Be on time; I don't want
to spoil the surprise.

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:44.135
I expect both of you
to show up.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.404
I'll be busy here.

00:05:45.478 --> 00:05:46.775
What's wrong, Seven?

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:49.076
No baby showers
in the collective?

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:51.776
I'm sure you can
spare a few minutes.

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:57.052
If it's any consolation,

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:59.785
I share your discomfort
with social gatherings.

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:02.054
They seem to occur
with alarming frequency.

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:06.087
Mr. Neelix would argue
that they improve morale.

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:09.896
I have been looking for ways
to improve my social skills.

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:13.005
Perhaps I'll attend.

00:06:13.072 --> 00:06:17.065
Well, it certainly is,
uh... efficient.

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:19.634
No clutter.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:24.581
Plenty of room to move around.

00:06:25.852 --> 00:06:28.047
Eh, but it's
a little impersonal.

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:29.383
Don't you think?

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:31.047
Explain.

00:06:31.124 --> 00:06:33.115
Well, these are your quarters,
Seven.

00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:35.319
They should reflect
your individuality.

00:06:35.395 --> 00:06:38.853
How about a table
and a couple of chairs?

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:40.660
Give yourself a place to work...

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:42.257
entertain guests.

00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:45.736
Uh, try to add a little color.

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:48.899
Uh, uh, photographs, uh,
artwork, knickknacks.

00:06:48.975 --> 00:06:49.942
Knickknacks?

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:50.941
Little things,

00:06:51.077 --> 00:06:53.944
like the wood carvings
in Ensign Kim's quarters.

00:06:54.013 --> 00:06:56.743
I've never been
to Ensign Kim's quarters.

00:06:56.816 --> 00:06:58.909
But I suppose I could
replicate some items

00:06:58.985 --> 00:07:00.885
and disperse them
throughout the room.

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:02.580
That's a start.

00:07:02.655 --> 00:07:06.113
Some people like to display
pictures of family and friends.

00:07:06.192 --> 00:07:07.682
There's a photograph
of my parents

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:08.749
in the ship's database.

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:10.523
I'll make a copy
and place it in a frame.

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:11.722
Good, good.

00:07:11.798 --> 00:07:15.894
A multispectral starchart
might enhance this bulkhead.

00:07:16.035 --> 00:07:17.832
Or a painting.

00:07:17.904 --> 00:07:19.428
A painting of a starchart.

00:07:19.505 --> 00:07:22.065
I-I was thinking of something
more abstract,

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:24.109
more, uh, artistic.

00:07:24.177 --> 00:07:25.474
Uh, drapes.

00:07:25.545 --> 00:07:28.844
Nothing livens up a room
like good window dressing.

00:07:28.915 --> 00:07:31.008
Not to mention
the added privacy.

00:07:31.083 --> 00:07:32.015
Privacy?

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:33.676
We're in space.

00:07:33.753 --> 00:07:34.777
Well, you never know

00:07:34.854 --> 00:07:36.754
when we'll be docking
at a crowded spaceport.

00:07:36.823 --> 00:07:40.589
But we'll have to make sure
that they match the carpet.

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:43.026
I'm thinking
of a Talaxian mosaic, uh,

00:07:43.095 --> 00:07:45.325
tulaberry blue stripes
with an orange inlay...

00:07:45.398 --> 00:07:47.263
I appreciate
your aesthetic insights,

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:50.564
but I believe I can
proceed on my own.

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:52.103
Enter.

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:55.568
Am I interrupting?

00:07:55.641 --> 00:07:57.370
Please come in.

00:07:57.443 --> 00:08:00.776
Love what you've done
with the place.

00:08:00.847 --> 00:08:02.212
We're in the process
of decorating.

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:05.739
Maybe this will help.

00:08:05.818 --> 00:08:08.116
Consider it a housewarming gift.

00:08:08.187 --> 00:08:09.779
It's beautiful.
What is it?

00:08:09.856 --> 00:08:10.880
A dreamcatcher.

00:08:10.957 --> 00:08:12.686
According to Native
American mythology,

00:08:12.758 --> 00:08:15.249
it wards off nightmares.

00:08:15.328 --> 00:08:16.556
I'm impressed.

00:08:16.629 --> 00:08:20.360
I've familiarized myself
with your culture.

00:08:20.433 --> 00:08:23.197
Now that you'll be sleeping
instead of regenerating,

00:08:23.269 --> 00:08:25.032
I thought it might
come in handy.

00:08:25.104 --> 00:08:26.799
I'm sure it will.

00:08:26.873 --> 00:08:28.033
Thank you.

00:08:28.107 --> 00:08:31.338
I'll let you two
find a place to hang that.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:36.211
But it would look perfect
right above the bed.

00:08:36.282 --> 00:08:38.807
Pleasant dreams.

00:08:41.921 --> 00:08:43.889
It was thoughtful
of you to stop by.

00:08:43.956 --> 00:08:44.888
On move-in day?

00:08:44.957 --> 00:08:45.889
I wouldn't miss it.

00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:48.051
I suppose this makes you
my inaugural guest.

00:08:48.127 --> 00:08:50.595
I'd be a negligent host

00:08:50.663 --> 00:08:52.096
if I didn't offer you
a beverage.

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:53.153
Tea?

00:08:53.232 --> 00:08:56.861
That might be difficult.

00:08:56.936 --> 00:08:58.927
No replicator.

00:08:59.005 --> 00:09:00.836
Another flaw in the decor.

00:09:00.907 --> 00:09:02.340
I'll requisition one

00:09:02.408 --> 00:09:03.966
for you first thing tomorrow.

00:09:04.043 --> 00:09:06.307
I'd appreciate that, Commander.

00:09:06.379 --> 00:09:09.075
Chakotay.

00:09:09.148 --> 00:09:10.274
We're off-duty.

00:09:10.349 --> 00:09:12.613
We can drop the formalities.

00:09:12.685 --> 00:09:13.709
Yes, sir.

00:09:14.987 --> 00:09:17.979
I enjoyed your toast today.

00:09:18.057 --> 00:09:20.617
You've come a long way.

00:09:20.693 --> 00:09:22.126
I hope to see more.

00:09:22.194 --> 00:09:24.788
You will.

00:09:26.432 --> 00:09:28.297
Good night.

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:30.267
Chakotay.

00:09:30.336 --> 00:09:32.099
As you might know,

00:09:32.171 --> 00:09:34.867
I've taken an interest
in culinary science.

00:09:34.941 --> 00:09:37.205
I'm preparing a meal
tomorrow night,

00:09:37.276 --> 00:09:39.904
and I thought perhaps
you could attend...

00:09:40.012 --> 00:09:41.809
to evaluate my work.

00:09:41.881 --> 00:09:43.439
I'd be happy to.

00:09:43.516 --> 00:09:45.108
1900 hours?

00:09:45.184 --> 00:09:47.277
I'll bring the wine...
and the furniture.

00:09:47.353 --> 00:09:48.877
Then you accept?

00:09:48.955 --> 00:09:50.980
It's a date.

00:10:01.567 --> 00:10:05.094
Rock-a-bye baby,
in the space dock

00:10:05.171 --> 00:10:08.607
When the core blows,
the shuttle will rock

00:10:08.674 --> 00:10:11.666
When the hull breaks,
the shuttle will fall

00:10:11.744 --> 00:10:15.373
And down will come baby,
shuttle and all...

00:10:15.448 --> 00:10:17.848
Are you trying to soothe
the infant or traumatize her?

00:10:17.917 --> 00:10:20.044
The lyrics are rather grim,

00:10:20.119 --> 00:10:21.814
but it's the melody
they respond to.

00:10:21.887 --> 00:10:23.912
I recorded 29 in all,

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:26.185
including a couple
of Klingon lullabies.

00:10:26.258 --> 00:10:29.750
My favorite is
"quong vaj Ocht."

00:10:29.829 --> 00:10:31.763
"Sleep, Little Warrior."

00:10:31.831 --> 00:10:33.890
I could tell by the look
on their faces

00:10:33.966 --> 00:10:35.957
that my gift made
quite an impression.

00:10:36.068 --> 00:10:37.535
No doubt.

00:10:37.603 --> 00:10:38.661
I wish you'd been there.

00:10:38.738 --> 00:10:39.762
It was a lovely shower.

00:10:39.839 --> 00:10:41.864
Tom and B'Elanna
were disappointed

00:10:41.941 --> 00:10:43.340
that you didn't attend.

00:10:43.409 --> 00:10:45.104
I was occupied.

00:10:45.177 --> 00:10:48.442
Are you experiencing
any shoulder pain?

00:10:48.514 --> 00:10:49.606
Yes.

00:10:49.682 --> 00:10:50.808
Hmm.

00:10:50.883 --> 00:10:53.545
Your biradial clamp is out
of alignment by.3 microns.

00:10:53.619 --> 00:10:55.450
I'm afraid it'll have
to be repaired.

00:10:55.521 --> 00:10:57.716
Can't you simply extract
the component?

00:10:57.790 --> 00:11:00.224
Not if you want to keep
using that arm.

00:11:01.494 --> 00:11:03.928
I know it's an inconvenience,
but until we can find a way

00:11:04.063 --> 00:11:05.587
to remove
your cybernetic systems,

00:11:05.665 --> 00:11:07.064
they'll have to be maintained.

00:11:07.133 --> 00:11:09.363
It's a minor procedure.

00:11:09.435 --> 00:11:11.494
We might as well
take care of it now.

00:11:11.570 --> 00:11:12.502
I prefer to wait.

00:11:12.571 --> 00:11:13.902
We'll be done in an hour.

00:11:13.973 --> 00:11:15.531
I have research to complete.

00:11:15.608 --> 00:11:17.769
Oh.

00:11:17.843 --> 00:11:21.802
I suppose we can put it off
until next week's physical.

00:11:21.881 --> 00:11:24.941
I also noticed that
your electrolyte levels

00:11:25.051 --> 00:11:26.211
are down by 12 percent.

00:11:26.285 --> 00:11:29.413
Have you missed any
regeneration cycles?

00:11:29.488 --> 00:11:30.819
Last night.

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:32.448
Don't tell me.

00:11:32.525 --> 00:11:33.514
More...

00:11:33.592 --> 00:11:35.560
research?

00:11:35.628 --> 00:11:37.960
This must be some project.

00:11:38.064 --> 00:11:40.089
Mind if I ask
what you're working on?

00:11:40.166 --> 00:11:41.098
It's complicated.

00:11:41.167 --> 00:11:42.099
How do you mean?

00:11:42.168 --> 00:11:44.830
My personal life is
none of your concern.

00:11:47.573 --> 00:11:50.007
I wasn't aware you
had a personal life.

00:11:51.377 --> 00:11:52.537
Report?

00:11:52.611 --> 00:11:55.978
It was an energy discharge,
200,000 kilometers starboard.

00:11:56.115 --> 00:11:58.583
It produced
a level-9 shock wave.

00:11:58.651 --> 00:11:59.879
Some kind of weapon?

00:11:59.952 --> 00:12:01.283
Possibly.

00:12:01.353 --> 00:12:03.583
Another one, five million
kilometers to port.

00:12:03.656 --> 00:12:05.647
A shock wave is approaching.

00:12:05.725 --> 00:12:08.159
Full power to the shields.

00:12:13.332 --> 00:12:16.130
Our warp field's destabilizing.

00:12:16.202 --> 00:12:17.692
I'm detecting another.

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:19.670
Distance: 50,000 kilometers.

00:12:19.739 --> 00:12:21.832
Turn our bow
into the wave front.

00:12:21.907 --> 00:12:23.101
It'll minimize the damage.

00:12:24.076 --> 00:12:26.670
Sorry, Captain,
there wasn't enough time.

00:12:26.746 --> 00:12:28.270
We've lost warp drive.

00:12:28.347 --> 00:12:29.746
I'm reading another.

00:12:29.815 --> 00:12:31.544
Distance:
26 million kilometers.

00:12:31.617 --> 00:12:32.948
Too far to pose a threat.

00:12:33.085 --> 00:12:34.279
If they are weapons,

00:12:34.353 --> 00:12:36.685
they don't seem
to be directed at us.

00:12:36.756 --> 00:12:39.350
Or whoever's firing them
is a lousy shot.

00:12:39.425 --> 00:12:43.486
Astrometric sensors
recorded the explosions.

00:12:43.562 --> 00:12:46.156
I believe it's
a long-range subspace warhead.

00:12:46.232 --> 00:12:48.427
The debris in this region

00:12:48.501 --> 00:12:49.729
suggests that dozens
have been fired

00:12:49.802 --> 00:12:50.962
in the last several weeks.

00:12:51.103 --> 00:12:52.627
The warhead destroyed something.

00:12:52.705 --> 00:12:53.637
What was it?

00:12:53.706 --> 00:12:55.298
It appeared to be
an unmanned probe.

00:12:55.374 --> 00:12:56.636
This is all very intriguing,

00:12:56.709 --> 00:12:58.370
but I'd just as soon
get out of here

00:12:58.444 --> 00:13:01.072
before we cross paths with
another one of these things.

00:13:01.147 --> 00:13:02.546
Where do we stand on repairs?

00:13:02.615 --> 00:13:04.549
Subspace radiation
from the explosions

00:13:04.617 --> 00:13:07.415
is making it difficult
to create a stable warp field.

00:13:07.486 --> 00:13:09.420
Lieutenant Torres
estimates 48 hours.

00:13:09.488 --> 00:13:11.649
Can you find a way
to detect the warheads

00:13:11.724 --> 00:13:13.487
before they emerge
from subspace?

00:13:13.559 --> 00:13:14.548
I believe so.

00:13:14.627 --> 00:13:16.595
The weapons create
minor gravimetric distortions

00:13:16.662 --> 00:13:18.027
as they approach
the subspace barrier,

00:13:18.097 --> 00:13:20.361
but I'll need to recalibrate
my sensors

00:13:20.432 --> 00:13:21.729
to isolate the effect.

00:13:21.801 --> 00:13:24.031
Do it. Even a few seconds'
warning would help us.

00:13:24.103 --> 00:13:26.765
Yes, Captain.

00:13:33.145 --> 00:13:35.636
Your duty shift doesn't
begin for two hours.

00:13:35.714 --> 00:13:38.080
The Doctor sent me
to relieve you early.

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:41.551
He wants you to spend
more time regenerating.

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:44.487
I see he's enlisted an ally.

00:13:44.557 --> 00:13:46.957
"Don't kill the messenger."

00:13:47.026 --> 00:13:49.426
It's Sophocles... Oedipus Rex.

00:13:49.495 --> 00:13:52.464
I've been studying
Earth literature

00:13:52.531 --> 00:13:54.761
as a part
of my Academy training.

00:13:56.368 --> 00:13:58.734
Continue these scans
of the subspace barrier.

00:13:58.804 --> 00:14:00.795
Look for any
gravimetric distortions.

00:14:26.098 --> 00:14:28.328
Run another diagnostic
on the injector ports.

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:29.697
Make sure they're aligned.

00:14:29.768 --> 00:14:31.099
They're aligned.
I checked.

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:32.137
Check again.

00:14:32.204 --> 00:14:33.398
Come to join the fun?

00:14:33.472 --> 00:14:35.940
We're trying to cold-start
the warp core...

00:14:36.008 --> 00:14:37.134
for the 15th time.

00:14:37.209 --> 00:14:39.769
Perhaps this will
enhance your day.

00:14:39.845 --> 00:14:42.905
It's a belated gift
for your baby shower.

00:14:42.982 --> 00:14:45.576
I apologize for my absence.

00:14:45.651 --> 00:14:47.209
Oh.

00:14:47.286 --> 00:14:48.947
Proceed.

00:14:53.092 --> 00:14:55.356
They're lined
with biothermal insulation.

00:14:55.427 --> 00:14:57.395
Your infant's feet
will be protected,

00:14:57.463 --> 00:14:59.522
even if the external
temperature drops

00:14:59.598 --> 00:15:01.293
below minus 40 degrees Celsius.

00:15:01.367 --> 00:15:04.700
Well, they're certainly unique.

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:06.135
Thank you.

00:15:06.205 --> 00:15:07.502
You're welcome.

00:15:12.111 --> 00:15:14.102
I wish to ask you
a personal question.

00:15:14.179 --> 00:15:15.976
Shoot.

00:15:19.385 --> 00:15:22.377
You have an appealing coiffure.

00:15:22.454 --> 00:15:23.887
What is your grooming regimen?

00:15:24.957 --> 00:15:28.324
You're asking me what
I do with my hair?

00:15:28.394 --> 00:15:29.884
Yes.

00:15:29.962 --> 00:15:33.762
Oh, well, nothing too elaborate.

00:15:33.832 --> 00:15:38.326
Sonic shower...
a little engine grease.

00:15:38.404 --> 00:15:39.837
Thinking about a new look?

00:15:39.905 --> 00:15:40.929
Perhaps.

00:15:41.006 --> 00:15:43.304
I'll keep you apprised
if you'd like.

00:15:43.375 --> 00:15:45.036
Please do.

00:15:49.114 --> 00:15:50.581
Was that Seven of Nine?

00:15:50.649 --> 00:15:53.812
There must be an alien
intruder on board.

00:15:56.088 --> 00:15:59.524
Computer, make the following
modifications to holodeck file:

00:15:59.591 --> 00:16:02.355
Seven of Nine Alpha-3,
Personal Quarters.

00:16:02.428 --> 00:16:04.726
Modifications complete.

00:16:04.797 --> 00:16:05.821
Begin program.

00:16:20.679 --> 00:16:23.079
You look perfect.

00:16:23.148 --> 00:16:24.945
Give me a hand with this?

00:16:26.618 --> 00:16:28.916
I'm surprised
your Starfleet training

00:16:29.021 --> 00:16:30.921
didn't include cork extraction.

00:16:31.023 --> 00:16:33.787
I must have been sick that day.

00:16:38.263 --> 00:16:40.197
Looks like wine's off the menu.

00:16:40.265 --> 00:16:42.392
Unless you brought a phaser.

00:16:42.468 --> 00:16:44.698
Never on the first date.

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:47.261
Assist me.

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:56.580
Slice these vegetables
transversally

00:16:56.648 --> 00:16:58.343
in five-millimeter increments.

00:16:58.417 --> 00:17:00.749
Aye, aye.

00:17:00.819 --> 00:17:02.252
That smells delicious.

00:17:02.321 --> 00:17:04.983
Our appetizer is braised leeks.

00:17:05.057 --> 00:17:08.823
Primary course: Rack of lamb
with wild rice.

00:17:08.894 --> 00:17:10.418
No dessert?

00:17:10.496 --> 00:17:13.294
Dessert will be a surprise.

00:17:15.601 --> 00:17:17.125
I can't wait.

00:17:17.202 --> 00:17:20.660
Does this contain enough
sodium chloride for your taste?

00:17:29.448 --> 00:17:32.542
Could use another
.6 milligrams,

00:17:32.618 --> 00:17:34.085
but you're the chef.

00:17:42.761 --> 00:17:45.025
I concur. More salt.

00:17:52.838 --> 00:17:54.066
Liszt?

00:17:54.139 --> 00:17:55.697
Chopin.

00:17:55.774 --> 00:17:57.674
I've discovered
that classical music

00:17:57.743 --> 00:17:59.870
has intriguing
mathematical properties.

00:17:59.945 --> 00:18:01.071
Do you play an instrument?

00:18:01.146 --> 00:18:03.637
The Doctor's been
giving me piano lessons.

00:18:03.715 --> 00:18:06.047
I'd love to hear you play.

00:18:06.118 --> 00:18:08.678
I require more practice.

00:18:13.625 --> 00:18:15.855
Your technique is flawed.

00:18:15.928 --> 00:18:18.795
Sorry. I'm a replicator man.

00:18:18.864 --> 00:18:21.662
Use your left hand
to guide the food.

00:18:24.937 --> 00:18:26.996
Observe closely.

00:18:34.646 --> 00:18:36.841
Pay attention to the vegetable.

00:18:36.915 --> 00:18:39.383
You're beautiful
when you're chopping.

00:18:57.269 --> 00:19:01.000
I don't mean to sound
like an old holonovel,

00:19:01.073 --> 00:19:03.268
but you've got
a wonderful smile.

00:19:03.342 --> 00:19:07.870
It wasn't a smile;
it was a smirk.

00:19:07.946 --> 00:19:09.208
Oh, no, it was a smile.

00:19:09.281 --> 00:19:12.512
I could check the internal
sensors if you'd like.

00:19:15.687 --> 00:19:17.951
Remain still.

00:19:31.103 --> 00:19:33.469
You have an intriguing
facial structure.

00:19:36.041 --> 00:19:37.702
I'll take that as a compliment.

00:20:10.909 --> 00:20:14.174
I require more practice.

00:20:14.246 --> 00:20:16.544
You're doing just fine.

00:20:21.787 --> 00:20:23.550
What's wrong?

00:20:25.724 --> 00:20:27.783
Nothing.

00:20:52.684 --> 00:20:54.845
I wasn't aware
you had a personal life.

00:21:12.771 --> 00:21:15.865
Chakotay to Seven of Nine.

00:21:15.941 --> 00:21:20.105
Chakotay to Seven.
Respond.

00:21:20.178 --> 00:21:21.440
Go ahead.

00:21:21.513 --> 00:21:22.946
Report to Astrometrics.

00:21:23.081 --> 00:21:24.844
We've found something.

00:21:24.916 --> 00:21:27.077
Yes, Commander.

00:21:32.024 --> 00:21:33.821
Good morning.

00:21:45.537 --> 00:21:47.698
Good morning.

00:21:49.441 --> 00:21:50.499
You found something.

00:21:50.575 --> 00:21:51.542
At first we thought

00:21:51.610 --> 00:21:53.305
it was another one
of the probes,

00:21:53.378 --> 00:21:55.846
then Icheb picked up
an automated transmission.

00:21:55.914 --> 00:21:58.314
It's a warning beacon.

00:21:58.383 --> 00:22:03.514
You have entered
Subspace Munitions Range 434.

00:22:03.588 --> 00:22:05.749
Evacuate immediately.

00:22:05.824 --> 00:22:10.124
Apparently, this entire region
is an alien testing ground.

00:22:10.195 --> 00:22:11.890
We've been sending
out emergency hails,

00:22:11.963 --> 00:22:13.021
but so far, no response.

00:22:13.098 --> 00:22:14.292
Whoever's conducting
these tests

00:22:14.366 --> 00:22:16.095
could be dozens
of light-years away.

00:22:16.168 --> 00:22:19.331
Any progress detecting
their warheads?

00:22:19.404 --> 00:22:20.735
Not yet.

00:22:25.677 --> 00:22:26.837
You seem a little distracted.

00:22:26.912 --> 00:22:27.936
I'm fine.

00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:31.447
It's not like you
to be late for a duty shift.

00:22:31.516 --> 00:22:33.143
Rough night?

00:22:33.218 --> 00:22:35.778
Not at all.

00:22:35.854 --> 00:22:39.346
I'll be on the Bridge
if you find anything.

00:22:42.994 --> 00:22:45.155
"Better late than never."

00:22:45.230 --> 00:22:46.959
Titus Livius,
A History of Rome.

00:22:47.032 --> 00:22:48.124
You're relieved.

00:22:52.137 --> 00:22:53.604
Get some rest.

00:23:28.507 --> 00:23:29.531
Bravo.

00:23:29.608 --> 00:23:30.666
You approve?

00:23:30.742 --> 00:23:33.939
Approve? I'm amazed.

00:23:34.079 --> 00:23:35.842
I was expecting "Chopsticks."

00:23:35.914 --> 00:23:37.472
I had no idea you were so good.

00:23:37.549 --> 00:23:40.313
The Doctor's
an efficient instructor.

00:23:40.385 --> 00:23:41.477
It won't be long

00:23:41.553 --> 00:23:44.147
before you're giving a recital
for the entire crew.

00:23:44.222 --> 00:23:46.713
The Doctor did suggest
that I accompany him

00:23:46.792 --> 00:23:49.955
during his next
operatic performance.

00:23:50.061 --> 00:23:52.086
Your turn.

00:23:52.164 --> 00:23:55.531
Mmm... unfortunately,
I don't play.

00:23:55.600 --> 00:23:57.591
But I'd love to hear you again.

00:23:57.669 --> 00:24:00.399
And this...

00:24:00.472 --> 00:24:01.962
is one of my favorites.

00:24:27.933 --> 00:24:29.093
You want me to stop?

00:24:29.167 --> 00:24:32.694
No. I want you to play.

00:24:32.771 --> 00:24:36.104
I don't understand.

00:24:36.174 --> 00:24:37.038
Look.

00:24:37.108 --> 00:24:39.736
Your technique is flawless,

00:24:39.811 --> 00:24:42.746
but try to put a little
more heart into the piece.

00:24:42.814 --> 00:24:44.372
More of yourself.

00:24:56.428 --> 00:24:57.395
That's all right.

00:24:57.462 --> 00:25:00.397
Keep going.

00:25:08.273 --> 00:25:10.036
Tell me what you're feeling.

00:25:10.108 --> 00:25:11.268
My tempo is erratic.

00:25:11.343 --> 00:25:12.605
Not what you're thinking.

00:25:12.677 --> 00:25:15.612
What you're feeling.

00:25:15.680 --> 00:25:17.511
Your emotions.

00:25:17.582 --> 00:25:19.812
Frustration, anxiety.

00:25:19.885 --> 00:25:21.147
Stop thinking about the notes.

00:25:21.219 --> 00:25:22.481
Just play.

00:25:23.889 --> 00:25:24.947
I can't.

00:25:26.391 --> 00:25:27.915
Yes, you can.

00:25:27.993 --> 00:25:29.927
Don't you see what's happening?

00:25:30.061 --> 00:25:32.552
The metronome
is holding you back.

00:25:32.631 --> 00:25:33.928
It gives you a sense of order,

00:25:33.999 --> 00:25:36.058
but it also cuts you
off from your feelings.

00:25:37.836 --> 00:25:39.929
Remember
when you first came aboard?

00:25:40.038 --> 00:25:42.233
The thought of disconnecting

00:25:42.307 --> 00:25:44.070
from the hive mind
terrified you.

00:25:44.142 --> 00:25:46.804
This is no different.

00:25:46.878 --> 00:25:48.971
It doesn't have to be perfect.

00:26:26.851 --> 00:26:30.014
800,000 kilometers
off the starboard bow.

00:26:30.088 --> 00:26:31.612
Bridge to Seven of Nine.

00:26:31.690 --> 00:26:32.816
Go ahead, Commander.

00:26:32.891 --> 00:26:34.620
We need
those sensor calibrations.

00:26:34.693 --> 00:26:37.560
I'll need a moment
to return to my station.

00:26:37.629 --> 00:26:39.620
That would be a good idea.

00:26:48.340 --> 00:26:51.173
Hull fracture, Deck 12.

00:26:51.242 --> 00:26:52.834
Seven of Nine, report.

00:26:52.911 --> 00:26:54.208
Stand by, Captain.

00:26:56.081 --> 00:26:59.949
Lieutenant Paris, isolate
subspace band omicron theta.

00:27:00.085 --> 00:27:01.848
Acknowledged.

00:27:01.920 --> 00:27:04.718
Direct your sensors
to coordinates 178 mark 26.

00:27:06.324 --> 00:27:07.348
Nothing there.

00:27:08.927 --> 00:27:11.657
Correction: 178 mark 36.

00:27:12.697 --> 00:27:14.062
I can see them.

00:27:14.132 --> 00:27:15.997
Two warheads
are about to emerge.

00:27:16.067 --> 00:27:17.056
Adjusting course.

00:27:17.135 --> 00:27:19.365
Full power
to the forward shields.

00:27:19.437 --> 00:27:21.064
Impact in five...

00:27:21.139 --> 00:27:22.868
four... three...

00:27:22.941 --> 00:27:24.499
two...

00:27:30.281 --> 00:27:31.680
Shields are holding.

00:27:31.750 --> 00:27:33.911
Why wasn't Seven at her post?

00:27:33.985 --> 00:27:34.917
Good question.

00:27:35.020 --> 00:27:35.987
Maybe you should ask her.

00:27:37.922 --> 00:27:40.720
It was your responsibility

00:27:40.792 --> 00:27:42.282
to locate those warheads.

00:27:42.360 --> 00:27:43.292
I succeeded.

00:27:43.361 --> 00:27:44.692
Not before we took
heavy damage.

00:27:44.763 --> 00:27:47.027
You told Chakotay you'd have
those sensor calibrations

00:27:47.098 --> 00:27:49.066
hours ago.

00:27:49.134 --> 00:27:51.602
The work took longer
than I anticipated.

00:27:51.670 --> 00:27:54.161
It might've gone faster
if you'd stayed at your post,

00:27:54.239 --> 00:27:55.536
as you were ordered to do.

00:27:55.607 --> 00:27:58.770
I didn't realize I was confined
to the Astrometrics Lab.

00:27:58.843 --> 00:28:00.936
You were on duty.

00:28:03.181 --> 00:28:05.615
This isn't the first time
you've left your station

00:28:05.684 --> 00:28:07.652
over the past few days.

00:28:07.719 --> 00:28:09.687
Holodeck 2?

00:28:09.754 --> 00:28:12.348
You've logged a lot
of time in there.

00:28:12.424 --> 00:28:13.891
Mind if I ask why?

00:28:15.927 --> 00:28:18.361
Well, it must be something
important, Seven.

00:28:19.998 --> 00:28:22.865
49 hours in six days?

00:28:22.934 --> 00:28:24.629
I was running a simulation.

00:28:24.703 --> 00:28:26.364
Of what?

00:28:30.542 --> 00:28:33.204
A new gravimetric array
I've been developing.

00:28:33.278 --> 00:28:37.214
I wanted to perfect the design
before I brought it to you.

00:28:37.282 --> 00:28:39.807
I appreciate your efforts
to improve our systems,

00:28:39.884 --> 00:28:42.546
but I can't have you
dividing your time right now.

00:28:42.620 --> 00:28:43.746
When the ship's on alert,

00:28:43.822 --> 00:28:45.551
I expect you
to perform your duties.

00:28:45.623 --> 00:28:48.251
If you need to leave your post,
inform Commander Chakotay.

00:28:48.326 --> 00:28:49.258
Understood?

00:28:49.327 --> 00:28:51.192
Yes, Captain.

00:28:51.262 --> 00:28:54.060
I apologize for my lapse
in judgment.

00:28:54.132 --> 00:28:57.465
We all make mistakes, Seven.

00:28:57.535 --> 00:29:00.129
I've even been known
to make a few myself.

00:29:03.708 --> 00:29:05.767
It sounds intriguing.

00:29:05.844 --> 00:29:08.074
Your new gravimetric array.

00:29:08.146 --> 00:29:11.081
When this crisis is over,
I'd be happy to take a look.

00:29:11.149 --> 00:29:13.276
Maybe I can lend a hand.

00:29:29.267 --> 00:29:32.862
I've analyzed the sensor data
from that last barrage.

00:29:32.937 --> 00:29:35.235
I've refined
your detection method.

00:29:38.376 --> 00:29:42.039
We'll be able to see the weapons
10.3 seconds earlier.

00:29:42.113 --> 00:29:44.047
The Captain will be pleased.

00:29:47.652 --> 00:29:49.279
Have I offended you?

00:29:53.191 --> 00:29:56.354
No. You've done nothing wrong.

00:29:59.798 --> 00:30:01.561
I was negligent in my duties.

00:30:01.633 --> 00:30:03.828
As a result, Voyager
was nearly destroyed.

00:30:06.371 --> 00:30:09.272
I was hoping you could
provide a quotation

00:30:09.340 --> 00:30:11.308
to help alleviate my guilt.

00:30:13.745 --> 00:30:15.838
I-I can't think of one,

00:30:15.914 --> 00:30:18.075
but I'd be happy
to search the database.

00:30:19.984 --> 00:30:21.918
That won't be necessary.

00:30:25.990 --> 00:30:27.958
Stay here until I return.

00:30:28.059 --> 00:30:28.821
Where are you going?

00:30:30.662 --> 00:30:32.653
To correct an error.

00:30:50.515 --> 00:30:53.575
Computer,
activate Chakotay simulation.

00:30:59.290 --> 00:31:00.518
Come in.

00:31:02.627 --> 00:31:04.492
I hope you're not allergic.

00:31:04.562 --> 00:31:06.257
Antarian moon blossoms.

00:31:06.331 --> 00:31:07.423
Extremely rare.

00:31:07.498 --> 00:31:09.523
I had to smuggle them
out of Airponics.

00:31:09.601 --> 00:31:11.899
Don't tell Neelix.

00:31:14.439 --> 00:31:16.930
I thought I'd cook
for you tonight.

00:31:17.008 --> 00:31:19.704
How does roasted chicken sound?

00:31:19.777 --> 00:31:23.474
I slaved over the replicator
for hours.

00:31:27.752 --> 00:31:29.242
Not hungry?

00:31:31.656 --> 00:31:34.250
I called you here to thank you.

00:31:34.325 --> 00:31:35.792
For what?

00:31:37.662 --> 00:31:40.893
The past few days
have been memorable.

00:31:42.500 --> 00:31:43.797
To say the least.

00:31:50.808 --> 00:31:51.968
You're ending this.

00:31:52.076 --> 00:31:55.671
In a manner of speaking, yes.

00:31:55.747 --> 00:31:57.806
Why?

00:31:57.882 --> 00:32:00.544
Our relationship is interfering

00:32:00.618 --> 00:32:02.347
with my responsibilities
on Voyager.

00:32:02.420 --> 00:32:03.853
I could speak to the Captain,

00:32:03.922 --> 00:32:05.753
have her cut back
on your duty shifts.

00:32:08.259 --> 00:32:10.557
Seven, the past few days
have been more than memorable.

00:32:10.628 --> 00:32:13.756
They've been an important
step forward for both of us.

00:32:13.831 --> 00:32:14.889
Don't throw that away.

00:32:14.966 --> 00:32:16.695
I'm sorry, Commander.

00:32:16.768 --> 00:32:18.759
You're making a mistake.

00:32:18.836 --> 00:32:22.294
No, I'm trying to correct one.

00:32:30.148 --> 00:32:33.311
Ask yourself why
you want to end this.

00:32:33.384 --> 00:32:35.249
Is it out of a sense of duty...

00:32:35.320 --> 00:32:36.912
or something else?

00:32:36.988 --> 00:32:39.252
Every time you move
closer to your emotions,

00:32:39.324 --> 00:32:40.416
you back away.

00:32:40.491 --> 00:32:42.083
Like hiding behind
that metronome.

00:32:42.160 --> 00:32:43.422
Your analogy is flawed.

00:32:43.494 --> 00:32:45.394
Is it?

00:32:45.463 --> 00:32:48.091
I think you're afraid
that embracing your humanity

00:32:48.166 --> 00:32:51.101
will make you weak,
less than perfect.

00:32:51.169 --> 00:32:53.194
But think about what
you stand to gain.

00:32:53.271 --> 00:32:54.203
It's irrelevant.

00:32:54.272 --> 00:32:55.864
No, it's not.

00:32:55.940 --> 00:32:58.408
Real intimacy
with another person...

00:32:58.476 --> 00:33:00.967
nothing's more relevant.

00:33:03.047 --> 00:33:04.571
I must return to my station.

00:33:04.649 --> 00:33:05.581
Stay here with me.

00:33:05.650 --> 00:33:06.776
This ship needs me.

00:33:06.851 --> 00:33:07.783
So do I.

00:33:08.853 --> 00:33:09.785
I can't function this way!

00:33:09.854 --> 00:33:11.185
You're not a drone
anymore, you're human!

00:33:11.255 --> 00:33:12.187
Stop!

00:33:13.658 --> 00:33:15.182
Seven!

00:33:15.259 --> 00:33:16.749
What's wrong?

00:33:21.499 --> 00:33:23.797
Sick Bay...

00:33:23.868 --> 00:33:25.096
medical emergency.

00:33:25.169 --> 00:33:26.966
Seven?

00:33:28.139 --> 00:33:30.073
Computer, locate Seven of Nine.

00:33:30.141 --> 00:33:32.769
Seven of Nine is in Holodeck 2.

00:33:38.082 --> 00:33:39.140
What happened?

00:33:39.217 --> 00:33:42.584
We were having an argument,
and she just collapsed.

00:33:42.653 --> 00:33:45.087
Her cortical node
is shutting down.

00:33:45.156 --> 00:33:46.589
She's going into neural shock.

00:33:46.657 --> 00:33:48.716
And what happened
to her facial implants?

00:33:48.793 --> 00:33:50.886
I thought you removed
all her cybernetic systems.

00:33:54.132 --> 00:33:56.259
Computer, end program.

00:34:18.289 --> 00:34:19.779
Commander?

00:34:19.857 --> 00:34:22.655
If you're looking for
your other holographic friend,

00:34:22.727 --> 00:34:24.285
he's off-line at the moment.

00:34:26.330 --> 00:34:28.798
Your cortical node
began to shut down.

00:34:28.866 --> 00:34:31.357
Fortunately, I managed
to stabilize it

00:34:31.436 --> 00:34:33.165
before there was
any permanent damage.

00:34:33.237 --> 00:34:34.499
It was functioning properly

00:34:34.572 --> 00:34:36.130
when you examined me
two days ago.

00:34:36.207 --> 00:34:39.108
I'm going to run a diagnostic
on your entire cortical array.

00:34:39.177 --> 00:34:41.509
But it might help if I
knew what you were doing,

00:34:41.579 --> 00:34:42.807
before you collapsed.

00:34:42.880 --> 00:34:45.542
Did you suffer a physical
injury of some kind?

00:34:45.616 --> 00:34:46.810
No.

00:34:46.884 --> 00:34:48.408
Were you exposed
to any unusual radiation?

00:34:48.486 --> 00:34:49.748
No.

00:34:49.821 --> 00:34:52.722
What exactly were you
doing in there?

00:34:54.892 --> 00:34:56.359
Research.

00:34:59.697 --> 00:35:02.097
That simulation
of Commander Chakotay

00:35:02.166 --> 00:35:05.624
mentioned that the two of you
were having an argument.

00:35:05.703 --> 00:35:10.333
Was that part of your research?

00:35:10.408 --> 00:35:12.069
I couldn't help but notice

00:35:12.143 --> 00:35:15.340
that you'd created some
quarters for yourself.

00:35:15.413 --> 00:35:19.509
A new dress...
dinner for two.

00:35:19.584 --> 00:35:25.045
I trust you'll respect
doctor-patient confidentiality.

00:35:25.123 --> 00:35:27.421
Of course.

00:35:30.061 --> 00:35:33.121
I've been conducting
simulations

00:35:33.197 --> 00:35:38.066
to explore different
aspects of my humanity.

00:35:38.136 --> 00:35:40.764
Such as?

00:35:40.838 --> 00:35:42.169
Social activities,

00:35:42.240 --> 00:35:45.573
friendships with the crew...

00:35:45.643 --> 00:35:47.611
intimate relations.

00:35:49.580 --> 00:35:54.142
I take it our First Officer
is your "romantic interest"?

00:35:54.218 --> 00:35:58.154
Commander Chakotay seemed
like an appropriate choice.

00:35:58.222 --> 00:36:01.089
He has many
admirable qualities.

00:36:01.159 --> 00:36:03.559
So he does.

00:36:03.628 --> 00:36:06.290
What prompted all this?

00:36:07.698 --> 00:36:09.097
Unimatrix Zero.

00:36:13.304 --> 00:36:15.033
I've been trying to re-create

00:36:15.106 --> 00:36:17.370
some of the experiences
I had there.

00:36:20.811 --> 00:36:24.770
Ever since it was destroyed,
my life has...

00:36:24.849 --> 00:36:27.181
seemed incomplete.

00:36:28.953 --> 00:36:32.286
I wanted to feel
those emotions again.

00:36:32.356 --> 00:36:33.914
Well...

00:36:34.025 --> 00:36:35.686
this is encouraging.

00:36:35.760 --> 00:36:37.250
You might be ready

00:36:37.328 --> 00:36:39.489
to start forming
deeper relationships.

00:36:39.564 --> 00:36:40.929
I'm proud of you, Seven.

00:36:41.032 --> 00:36:42.932
Your pride is misplaced.

00:36:43.034 --> 00:36:45.594
I intend to delete the programs.

00:36:45.670 --> 00:36:46.796
Why?

00:36:46.871 --> 00:36:49.499
I can no longer perform
my duties efficiently.

00:36:49.574 --> 00:36:51.940
My personal life has
become a distraction.

00:36:52.043 --> 00:36:53.908
It's supposed to be
a distraction.

00:36:53.978 --> 00:36:56.276
You simply have to find
the right balance

00:36:56.347 --> 00:36:58.076
between work and recreation.

00:36:58.149 --> 00:37:00.549
Inform me when you
finish the diagnostic.

00:37:00.618 --> 00:37:01.880
Seven.

00:37:01.953 --> 00:37:04.217
For what it's worth,

00:37:04.288 --> 00:37:06.984
you have excellent taste.

00:37:08.593 --> 00:37:11.391
Your quarters...

00:37:11.462 --> 00:37:13.623
they suited you.

00:37:27.211 --> 00:37:30.237
Antimatter flow: Stable.

00:37:30.314 --> 00:37:32.305
Injector ports: Aligned.

00:37:32.383 --> 00:37:34.248
That should do it.

00:37:34.318 --> 00:37:35.785
Torres to the Bridge.

00:37:35.853 --> 00:37:37.844
Looks like we've got
warp drive back.

00:37:37.922 --> 00:37:39.480
Well done. Tom.

00:37:39.557 --> 00:37:41.718
With pleasure.

00:37:47.965 --> 00:37:50.126
I'm detecting another
subspace warhead.

00:37:50.201 --> 00:37:51.828
Range?

00:37:51.902 --> 00:37:52.926
12 million kilometers.

00:37:53.070 --> 00:37:54.094
Closing from astern.

00:37:54.171 --> 00:37:55.160
Red Alert.

00:37:55.239 --> 00:37:56.501
Where's the target probe?

00:37:56.574 --> 00:37:58.906
It's on a totally
different trajectory.

00:37:58.976 --> 00:38:00.443
When we engaged the engines,

00:38:00.511 --> 00:38:03.002
the warhead must have diverted
from its target

00:38:03.080 --> 00:38:05.048
and locked on
to our warp signature.

00:38:05.116 --> 00:38:06.549
Evasive maneuvers.

00:38:06.617 --> 00:38:08.710
It's matching our course.

00:38:08.786 --> 00:38:10.117
Eight million kilometers.

00:38:10.187 --> 00:38:11.677
Can you get a weapons lock?

00:38:11.756 --> 00:38:13.189
Affirmative.

00:38:13.257 --> 00:38:15.452
Photon torpedoes.

00:38:15.526 --> 00:38:16.720
Full spread.

00:38:25.036 --> 00:38:27.470
Our torpedoes
have been neutralized.

00:38:27.538 --> 00:38:29.199
Five million kilometers.

00:38:29.273 --> 00:38:30.831
Bridge to Seven of Nine.

00:38:30.908 --> 00:38:31.840
Here, Captain.

00:38:31.909 --> 00:38:33.376
Can you get me anything

00:38:33.444 --> 00:38:35.378
on the warhead's
internal circuitry?

00:38:35.446 --> 00:38:36.777
Stand by.

00:38:37.982 --> 00:38:39.244
I have it.

00:38:39.317 --> 00:38:41.410
What can you tell me
about the detonator?

00:38:41.485 --> 00:38:42.452
The weapon is armed

00:38:42.520 --> 00:38:44.613
with proximity
resonance circuitry.

00:38:44.689 --> 00:38:46.680
What's the activation frequency?

00:38:46.757 --> 00:38:48.782
4.84 gigahertz.

00:38:48.859 --> 00:38:51.919
I may be able to disarm it
with an antiresonance pulse.

00:38:51.996 --> 00:38:52.928
Do it.

00:38:53.064 --> 00:38:54.122
Two million kilometers.

00:38:54.198 --> 00:38:55.460
Initiating the pulse.

00:38:55.533 --> 00:38:56.591
Seven, status?

00:38:56.667 --> 00:38:59.830
The warhead's rotating
its activation frequency.

00:38:59.904 --> 00:39:01.496
It's still armed.

00:39:01.572 --> 00:39:03.267
One million kilometers.

00:39:03.341 --> 00:39:04.399
Can you compensate?

00:39:04.475 --> 00:39:06.602
Negative.

00:39:06.677 --> 00:39:09.202
Captain, I believe
I can disarm the warhead.

00:39:09.280 --> 00:39:10.338
How?

00:39:10.414 --> 00:39:12.177
By extracting the detonator
with our transporter.

00:39:12.249 --> 00:39:13.511
At this velocity?

00:39:13.584 --> 00:39:15.017
The device is too small.

00:39:15.086 --> 00:39:16.519
You'd never get a lock.

00:39:16.587 --> 00:39:20.216
I can use the submicron imager
to focus our targeting scanners.

00:39:20.291 --> 00:39:22.691
Please, give me
transporter control.

00:39:25.463 --> 00:39:26.589
800,000.

00:39:27.998 --> 00:39:31.456
All right, Seven.
It's up to you.

00:39:31.535 --> 00:39:33.730
I have a lock.

00:39:33.804 --> 00:39:35.567
Energizing.

00:39:37.708 --> 00:39:40.472
The detonator's protected
by tritanium shielding.

00:39:40.544 --> 00:39:42.910
I can penetrate it,
but not at this distance.

00:39:43.013 --> 00:39:45.004
We'll have to wait
until it's closer.

00:39:45.082 --> 00:39:46.674
500,000.

00:39:46.751 --> 00:39:47.683
Status?

00:39:47.752 --> 00:39:48.719
Not yet, Captain.

00:39:48.786 --> 00:39:50.117
Four...

00:39:50.187 --> 00:39:51.654
three...

00:39:51.722 --> 00:39:52.848
two...

00:39:52.923 --> 00:39:55.653
Brace for impact!

00:40:06.971 --> 00:40:09.405
Doctor.

00:40:09.473 --> 00:40:12.840
You've come to deliver
unpleasant news.

00:40:12.910 --> 00:40:16.402
Is it that obvious?

00:40:16.480 --> 00:40:19.210
I've completed my diagnostic.

00:40:19.283 --> 00:40:23.117
What you experienced
was no malfunction.

00:40:23.187 --> 00:40:25.280
Your cortical node
was designed

00:40:25.356 --> 00:40:28.086
to shut down your
higher brain functions

00:40:28.159 --> 00:40:30.320
when you achieve
a certain level

00:40:30.394 --> 00:40:32.123
of emotional stimulation.

00:40:33.264 --> 00:40:34.856
Clarify.

00:40:34.932 --> 00:40:37.662
It appears to be
a fail-safe mechanism...

00:40:37.735 --> 00:40:40.067
to deactivate drones

00:40:40.137 --> 00:40:42.571
who start to regain
their emotions.

00:40:42.640 --> 00:40:45.632
Knowing the Borg, it
makes perfect sense.

00:40:45.709 --> 00:40:47.108
Finding one's heart

00:40:47.178 --> 00:40:49.840
is the surest road
to individuality.

00:40:49.914 --> 00:40:51.973
But I'm no longer linked
to the hive mind.

00:40:52.049 --> 00:40:54.074
The technology's
built into your node.

00:40:54.151 --> 00:40:57.279
It simply remained
dormant... until now.

00:41:01.892 --> 00:41:04.588
Can you repair me?

00:41:04.662 --> 00:41:06.562
Possibly.

00:41:06.630 --> 00:41:08.791
I've been thinking about a way

00:41:08.866 --> 00:41:11.835
to reconfigure
the micro-circuitry.

00:41:11.902 --> 00:41:14.598
I won't lie to you, Seven.

00:41:14.672 --> 00:41:17.505
It would entail
multiple surgeries,

00:41:17.575 --> 00:41:19.941
and the recovery
might be difficult.

00:41:20.077 --> 00:41:22.671
But I believe we could
eventually succeed.

00:41:22.746 --> 00:41:24.839
I'll prepare the Surgical Bay.

00:41:24.915 --> 00:41:25.939
We can begin tomorrow morning.

00:41:26.016 --> 00:41:27.506
No.

00:41:27.585 --> 00:41:30.554
Without the procedure,
you won't be able

00:41:30.621 --> 00:41:32.782
to continue your simulations.

00:41:32.857 --> 00:41:35.917
I've experienced enough
humanity for the time being.

00:41:35.993 --> 00:41:39.087
They were only
holographic fantasies, Doctor.

00:41:39.163 --> 00:41:40.960
An inefficient use of my time.

00:41:41.031 --> 00:41:42.396
You don't really believe that.

00:41:42.466 --> 00:41:43.956
The fail-safe device
will ensure

00:41:44.034 --> 00:41:45.661
that I'm no longer distracted.

00:41:45.736 --> 00:41:47.203
That's the Borg talking...

00:41:47.271 --> 00:41:48.704
not you.

00:41:48.772 --> 00:41:53.334
As your physician...
as your friend,

00:41:53.410 --> 00:41:55.469
I'm asking you
to let me proceed.

00:41:55.546 --> 00:41:56.877
I need to regenerate.

00:41:56.947 --> 00:41:58.175
Seven...

00:41:58.249 --> 00:41:59.682
Good night, Doctor.

00:42:16.333 --> 00:42:17.698
Where's the fire?

00:42:17.768 --> 00:42:18.700
Fire?

00:42:18.769 --> 00:42:20.293
You seem to be in a hurry.

00:42:20.371 --> 00:42:23.499
I have to finish my report
on the subspace warheads.

00:42:23.574 --> 00:42:25.439
The ship's out of danger,
thanks to you.

00:42:25.509 --> 00:42:26.498
You've earned a break.

00:42:26.577 --> 00:42:28.442
Why don't you join me
in the Mess Hall?

00:42:28.512 --> 00:42:30.571
Neelix is going to give
a cooking lesson:

00:42:30.648 --> 00:42:32.548
"Talaxian Tenderloin
in Ten Minutes."

00:42:32.616 --> 00:42:34.709
I'm no longer interested
in cooking.

00:42:34.785 --> 00:42:36.116
Then come for the company.

00:42:36.186 --> 00:42:37.744
B'Elanna's going to be there.

00:42:37.821 --> 00:42:39.482
Tuvok even promised to show up.

00:42:39.557 --> 00:42:41.548
It'll be fun.

00:42:41.625 --> 00:42:44.219
I appreciate your offer.

00:42:44.295 --> 00:42:46.058
Another time, perhaps.

00:42:46.130 --> 00:42:49.065
You know,
you should try socializing

00:42:49.133 --> 00:42:51.499
with the crew a little more.

00:42:51.569 --> 00:42:53.799
It might do you some good.
